# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
# Lumen OS for the XGIMI Play 6 (G0058): always-on settings (install as /system/etc/init/play6_base.rc,
# tools/play6/compose.sh). A fork of the Z9X's overlay/v1/z9x_base.rc with only its Bluetooth line
# (docs/play6/SETTINGS_PLAN.md step 13; tools/play6/forks.tsv, check F). Left out on purpose:
#  - the smart_ak_server stop rule: written for the G0082, where Perception_SmartAK is disabled; the Play 6
#    vendor ships and uses /vendor/bin/smart_ak_server.
#  - ro.audio.flinger_standbytime_ms 30000: tied to the Z9X lamp-off and STR.
#  - sys.z9x.feat 1: it turns on Z9X-only code paths.
# A further line comes here only after test A7 shows that it applies to the G0058; the Play 6-only block at the end
# (the Bluetooth role of the speaker mode, P3 item 21) is not part of the fork.
#
# Only init builtins (setprop), no exec, no wait: nothing here can delay early-boot. Bluetooth reads the
# privacy flag much later, when system_server enables the adapter.
#  - bluetooth.core.gap.le.privacy.enabled=false: public address, so the XGIMI BLE remote (000d:3841, the
#    same remote as the Z9X's) reconnects after a reboot without re-pairing.
on early-boot
    setprop bluetooth.core.gap.le.privacy.enabled false
    setprop sys.lumen.p6.bt_roles 1
    # Play 6 only: both A2DP roles at once (headphones as A2DP source and a phone playing to the projector as A2DP
    # sink), as stock Android 11 ran them, is OFF since Lumen OS 1.0.6. Android 14 runs both only with its
    # src_sink_coexist switch, and then the legacy AVRCP controller (btif_rc) takes the AVRCP channel a speaker opens
    # ("bta_av_rc_ctrl_cback: not cback legacy cback, and close the handle"): the owner's Yandex Station Street
    # (BlueZ) played its "disconnected" sound a second after every connect and stopped the sound, while Android still
    # showed it connected (2026-10-24, logcat). With the source role alone AVRCP stays up and absolute volume works.
    # The speaker mode switches the role itself (the triggers at the end of this file, speaker/BtRole). Opt in to
    # both roles again: setprop persist.lumen.p6.bt_coexist 1 and reboot.

# Play 6 only, Lumen OS 1.0.6: Bluetooth absolute volume on (the Z9X gets it from product_prop_v1.txt). The Play 6
# vendor init sets persist.bluetooth.disableabsvol=true very early (vendor_init audit on stock and on Lumen), so a
# build.prop line would lose; early-boot runs after it and before system_server starts Bluetooth. With it on, the
# remote's volume keys set the speaker's own volume (AVRCP), as on a phone. Speakers paired before keep their old
# record of the projector and may need to be paired again (BlueZ speakers cache it).
on early-boot
    setprop persist.bluetooth.disableabsvol false

on early-boot && property:persist.lumen.p6.bt_coexist=1
    setprop bluetooth.a2dp.src_sink_coexist.enabled true
    setprop bluetooth.profile.a2dp.sink.enabled true
    setprop bluetooth.profile.avrcp.controller.enabled true

# ---- Play 6 only, P3 item 21: the Bluetooth A2DP role of the speaker mode (org.z9x.projector speaker/BtRole,
# docs/play6/TASKS.md "P3 stock features"). The Bluetooth app of Android 14 reads these profile switches when its
# process starts; a platform app may not write bluetooth.profile.* itself, so the projector app writes
# sys.lumen.p6.bt_role and init applies the set, then the app restarts Bluetooth. "speaker": the projector is an
# A2DP sink with an AVRCP controller (a phone plays to it, the remote's media keys reach the phone), no A2DP source
# (no headphones meanwhile). "normal": the image values again (A2DP source for headphones, as before). The
# sys.* value is gone after a reboot, so every boot starts with the image values. sys.lumen.p6.bt_roles=1 (above)
# tells the app that this image has the triggers; without it the speaker mode is hidden.
on property:sys.lumen.p6.bt_role=speaker
    setprop bluetooth.profile.a2dp.source.enabled false
    setprop bluetooth.profile.a2dp.sink.enabled true
    setprop bluetooth.profile.avrcp.controller.enabled true

on property:sys.lumen.p6.bt_role=normal
    setprop bluetooth.profile.a2dp.sink.enabled false
    setprop bluetooth.profile.avrcp.controller.enabled false
    setprop bluetooth.profile.a2dp.source.enabled true
